<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 7.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-June 7.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended June 7</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>HDFC		  3315	   9.85	99400  329.51   15.49</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   172	   0.43     571750  180.10    7.12</p>
<p>State Bank	   315	   0.87     577900   10.69   61.30</p>
<p>SPIC		  18.5	   0.03     105000  117.60    0.14</p>
<p>ACC		   1120	   2.97	29210   32.72   13.83</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   890	   2.33	32150   28.61   13.65</p>
<p>MTNL		   270	   0.84     102600   27.70   16.22</p>
<p>Castrol		465	   1.33	57100   26.55   14.91</p>
<p>HLL		   1235	   3.40	21450   26.49   14.36</p>
<p>L &amp; T		  220	   0.62     117850   25.93   14.69</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 11.13 percent on an annualised basis against 8.91 percent in the previous carry forward account ended May 31.</p>
